<section id="overview">
  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>
    A self-contained terminal app for getting work done with an LLM. It
    speaks Anthropic's Claude API natively and any OpenAI-compatible
    endpoint (DeepSeek, OpenAI, OpenRouter, Together, local Ollama, …) for
    cheap delegation. It runs an autonomous tool-using loop with bash, file
    edit, glob, grep, and web fetch behind a permission system that prompts
    you only when you ask it to.
  </p>
  <p>
    The engine runs concurrent-safe tools in parallel via
    <code>tokio::spawn</code> and sequential ones in order. Context is
    compacted automatically at a 60% token threshold. File mutations are
    tracked on an undo stack, and provider overload triggers exponential
    backoff with up to 3 retries.
  </p>
  <ul class="bullets">
    <li><strong>Modern terminal UI</strong>: sidebar, command palette, model picker, session list, runtime theme switcher (rose-pine, catppuccin, tokyo-night, gruvbox), mouse + bracketed paste, <code>@</code>-file mentions, slash-command popover, toasts, and a colorized diff renderer.</li>
    <li><strong>Intern mode</strong>: a senior model delegates to one or more cheaper OpenAI-compatible models, each exposed as a <code>delegate_to_&lt;name&gt;</code> tool.</li>
    <li><strong>Permission-first</strong>: Normal / Auto-accept / Plan / Bypass modes with per-tool allow rules.</li>
    <li><strong>Skills as slash commands</strong>: drop a markdown file under <code>.claude/skills/</code> and it appears as <code>/your-skill</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Sessions</strong>: automatic per-project persistence.</li>
    <li><strong>Hooks</strong>: shell hooks for <code>session-start</code>, <code>pre-tool-use</code>, <code>post-tool-use</code>, and <code>stop</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="install">
  <h2>Installation</h2>
  <p>The installed binary is <code>stynx</code>. Published on crates.io.</p>
  <DocCode title="bash · fastest, from crates.io" lang="bash" code={`# install the latest release
cargo install stynx-code

# then run it
stynx`} />
  <DocCode title="bash · from source / with nix" lang="bash" code={`# from source
git clone https://github.com/maulanasdqn/stynx-code
cd stynx-code
cargo install --path stynx-code

# with nix
nix develop
cargo build --release --workspace
./target/release/stynx`} />
</section>

<section id="quickstart">
  <h2>Quickstart</h2>
  <p>Four ways to run, depending on whether you want the interactive UI or a scriptable one-shot.</p>
  <DocCode title="bash" lang="bash" code={`# interactive TUI (the main mode)
stynx

# one-shot prompt
stynx -p "find every TODO comment under src/ and group by file"

# pipe mode: read stdin as the prompt
echo "explain this file" | stynx

# JSON output for scripting
stynx --json -p "list files modified in the last commit"`} />
</section>

<section id="auth">
  <h2>Authentication</h2>
  <p>Anthropic credentials are resolved in this order, the first one found wins:</p>
  <ol class="bullets">
    <li>macOS Keychain / Linux libsecret (the Claude Code OAuth token at <code>Claude Code-credentials</code>)</li>
    <li><code>~/.stynx/.credentials.json</code></li>
    <li><code>~/.claude/.credentials.json</code> <em>(Claude Code compatible fallback)</em></li>
    <li><code>~/.stynx/settings.json</code> → <code>env.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN</code> (with optional <code>env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL</code>)</li>
    <li>The <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> environment variable</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Run <code>/login</code> inside <code>stynx</code> for interactive instructions, and <code>/logout</code> to clear credentials. Intern (OpenAI-compatible) keys are read from environment variables; see <a href="#interns">Intern mode</a>.</p>
</section>
